Title: Clean Pages
Credit: Written by
Author: Sample fixture (deliberately defect-free)
Contact: fixture@example.com

FADE IN:

INT. BOOKBINDERY - MORNING

Glue smell. Presses under dust sheets. NADIA (30s) squares a stack of
signatures against the bench, thumb testing every edge.

OSCAR (60s) unlocks the till without looking up.

OSCAR
You slept here.

NADIA
The Halloran job ships Thursday.

OSCAR
It shipped Tuesday. I sent it.

Nadia sets the stack down.

NADIA
Then what am I binding.

EXT. LOADING DOCK - MORNING

A van idles. Oscar wheels out a pallet. Nadia follows with the stack
still in her arms.

OSCAR
Something that pays.

NADIA
That's not an answer.

OSCAR
It's the one I've got.

He takes the stack from her and slides it onto the pallet.

INT. BOOKBINDERY - AFTERNOON

The dust sheets are off. Every press is running. Nadia works the
guillotine, feeding it steadily.

NADIA
How long have you known.

OSCAR
Since the letter.

NADIA
You didn't say.

OSCAR
You'd have finished it anyway.

She stops the guillotine. Looks at him.

INT. STOCKROOM - EVENING

Shelves to the ceiling. Nadia pulls a box down and finds it empty.
Oscar watches from the doorway.

OSCAR
Every one of them.

NADIA
I'll rebind them.

OSCAR
With what.

Nadia flattens the empty box against her chest.

NADIA
Thursday. Like I said.

FADE OUT.
